        "original_id": "809d17f9-697c-53de-a63e-439735d7fb36",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Organizations: Orlando Magic, Houston Rockets, National Basketball Association\n- Events: 1995 NBA Finals, 2009 NBA Finals, NBA playoffs\n- People: Morlon David Wiley\n- Places: Orlando, Florida\n\nFacts:\n- The Orlando Magic are an American professional basketball team based in Orlando, Florida.\n- Morlon David Wiley was born on September 24, 1966, and he is an American former professional basketball player.\n- The 1995 NBA Finals was the championship round of the 1994–95 National Basketball Association season.\n- The 1995 NBA Finals matched the Eastern Conference champion Orlando Magic against the Western Conference champion Houston Rockets.\n- The Orlando Magic reached the NBA Finals in 1995 and again in 2009.\n- As of 2017, the Orlando Magic had made 14 NBA playoff appearances in 28 years, which was exactly half of the franchise's existence.\n- Morlon David Wiley later served as an assistant coach for the National Basketball Association's Orlando Magic.",
